# Public ingress for a host that runs both Jitsi Meet and the Starry API.
#
# Topology it expects:
#   * Jitsi's web container is published on loopback in plain HTTP
#     (HTTP_PORT=127.0.0.1:8081 in the compose .env); it never terminates TLS.
#   * starry-api listens on 127.0.0.1:21114 and treats X-Forwarded-For as the
#     client address (STARRY_API_TRUST_PROXY=1).
#   * Caddy owns 80/443 for every name below and is the only ACME client, so
#     remove ENABLE_LETSENCRYPT from the container or let it lapse.
#
# Replace the host names with your own. RustDesk clients use the API host as
# their "API Server"; the ID/relay traffic stays on the 21115-21119 ports and
# does not pass through here.

meet.example.com, whiteboard.meet.example.com {
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=63072000"
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8081
}

# RustDesk-compatible accounts API (starry-api).
rustdesk.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:21114
}
